in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @magic
in @magic/contract
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/magic — the form/process-substrate-altitude adapter species.
# Bridges the @smarts family (substrate-architectural integration;
# #83) with the @magic family (form/process substrate-decl; #80)
# honestly via the adapter pattern, following the @smarts/pack
# precedent (tick 56) and the @magic/frame doubled-bilateral pattern
# (tick 27).
#
# Tick 58 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 57's residue:
# orchestra Seam consolidation landed (C1/C3/C9 closed); the cross-
# species `requires` mechanism surfaced the substrate-realisation gap
# honestly. This tick extends the @smarts cross-family adapter set
# the family-root explicitly forward-promised:
#
#   "Plus cross-family integration adapters following the @magic/
#    distinction pattern:
#    - shards/smarts/magic.mirror       — @smarts ↔ @magic adapter"
#                                         [THIS SHARD]
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# @smarts.smarts records carry `magic_form: magic_contract` as the
# first form field (per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4 closure). The
# typed-field already names the @magic identity at the @smarts
# integration altitude; this adapter EMPIRICALLY DISCHARGES the
# composition by exposing the bilateral predicate consumer species
# can name in `requires` clauses.
#
# Without this adapter, the magic_form: magic_contract field is
# substrate-decl'd as typed but the @magic discipline (invariant
# preservation) is not load-bearing at the @smarts integration
# boundary. With this adapter, the bilateral smarts_satisfies_magic
# routes BOTH families' verdicts through one `requires` clause.
#
# === The adapter pattern (per @smarts/pack template, tick 56) ===
#
# @magic's family-root carriers (per shards/magic.mirror #80):
#   - magic_surface     gauge-visible interface
#   - magic_mechanism   matter-hidden trick
#   - magic_invariant   the named promise
#   - magic_contract    record {surface, mechanism, promise}
#
# @smarts's family-root carriers (per shards/smarts.mirror #83):
#   - smarts            record {magic_form: magic_contract, frame_form,
#                               cyberpunk_form, beam_form,
#                               cybernetic_extra, kintsugi_form}
#   - deployment        record {form: smarts, host: ref, manifest: ref}
#
# The substrate-pull-correct mapping (already typed at @smarts
# carrier altitude; this adapter exposes the bilateral):
#
#   smarts.magic_form  ↔ magic_contract  (field-projection; this IS
#                                          the load-bearing identity)
#   smarts             ↔ magic-form-as-projection-of-integration
#
# === The doubled-bilateral structural shape ===
#
# Per @magic/frame + @smarts/pack templates: the bilateral predicate
# discharges TWO family predicates in one clause:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) (@smarts family-root): the substrate-
#      architectural-integration discipline verifier per #83.
#      Discharges that the @smarts integration maintains bilateral
#      discipline-flexibility under perturbation.
#
#   2. invariant_preserved(magic_form_of(s), smarts_promise(s))
#      (@magic/contract family): the form/process-substrate discipline
#      verifier per #80. Discharges that the @magic contract's promise
#      is preserved by the contract under the boundary harness at @io
#      per recognition #57.
#
# Both must hold for the smarts integration to satisfy @magic at the
# substrate altitude. The cross-family composition mechanically
# discharges the form/process-substrate-altitude identity claim.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994.
#                               Structural OO-canonical adapter;
#                               inherited via @magic/frame tick 27 +
#                               @smarts/pack tick 56.
#   functor adjunction          Mac Lane 1971. Category theory's
#                               mathematical ancestor of cross-family
#                               composition discipline preservation.
#   composition over            Coplien 1992; Gamma et al 1994. The
#   inheritance                 cultural-practice ancestor.
#   Clarke's third law          Clarke 1962. The cultural vocabulary
#                               @magic carries at substrate altitude;
#                               @smarts/magic threads that into the
#                               substrate-architectural integration.
#   knowledge commons           Ostrom 1990. The hosting-discipline
#                               ancestor of @smarts; @smarts/magic
#                               threads @magic's encapsulation into
#                               the common-goods integration boundary.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT make every @magic_contract automatically a @smarts
#    integration. The adapter is opt-in.
# 2. Does NOT absorb @magic into @smarts. The two families remain
#    distinct.
# 3. Does NOT discharge the magic_form-to-other-form bilateral
#    composition (frame_form, cyberpunk_form, etc. each need their
#    own @smarts/<family> adapters forward-promised by the
#    @smarts family-root).
# 4. Does NOT supersede @magic/frame's cognitive-altitude bridge
#    or @magic/distinction's Spencer-Brown-altitude adapter. Three
#    @magic adapters at three altitudes; orthogonal.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at form/process-substrate altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole adapter (honest): smarts_satisfies_magic returns
# SATISFIED only when BOTH bilaterals discharge substantively. The
# @smarts discipline_flexible AND the @magic invariant_preserved
# both hold under perturbation; the @smarts integration includes a
# @magic contract whose promise is honored substantively.
#
# Narcissus-pole adapter (deceptive): smarts_satisfies_magic returns
# SATISFIED while one or both bilaterals fail substantively. The
# @smarts integration claims @magic discipline via name-only (the
# magic_form field is populated but the promise is violated by the
# mechanism); the contract is gauge-visible but matter-hidden in a
# way that masks the violation.
#
# Per the @magic/frame + @smarts/pack precedent + #57: the adapter
# MUST NOT permit Narcissus-pole bypass. The bilateral's two
# `requires` clauses discharge to BOTH family predicates;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) at @io enforces the
# discrimination.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root;
#               declares the magic_form: magic_contract field this
#               adapter exposes);
#               shards/magic.mirror (the @magic family-root; the
#               form/process-substrate parent).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; the boundary harness at @io keeps the
#                       Splinter/Narcissus discrimination honest under
#                       the lift),
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                       (#55; @smarts and @magic as form-side at
#                       deployment and substrate altitudes
#                       respectively; this adapter threads them at
#                       the integration crossing),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]]
#                       (Reed's discipline; the bilateral makes the
#                       composition empirically discharged),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (smarts and
#                       perturbation taken as typed parameters at
#                       the bilateral signature).
# Related shards: smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root; the form-
#                  side at deployment altitude),
#                 magic.mirror (the @magic family-root; the form-
#                  side at substrate altitude),
#                 magic/contract.mirror (the consumer of
#                  invariant_preserved this adapter routes through),
#                 magic/frame.mirror (the cognitive-altitude adapter
#                  precedent at tick 27; this shard inherits the
#                  doubled-bilateral shape),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (the Spencer-Brown-
#                  altitude adapter precedent at tick 15),
#                 smarts/pack.mirror (the agent-runtime-altitude
#                  adapter precedent at tick 56; sibling cross-family
#                  adapter from the @smarts family-root forward-promise
#                  set).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/magic.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/magic` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/mathematics/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/programming/coplien-1992
source @arxiv/cultural/clarke-1962
source @arxiv/common-goods/ostrom-1990

prism @smarts/magic {
  focus magic
  project magic
  split magic
  shift magic
  settle magic
}

# === magic_form_of adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action projecting the @magic
# contract from a @smarts integration. The @smarts integration's
# magic_form field IS the @magic contract at the substrate altitude;
# this projection EXPOSES the field as a substrate-decl operation
# the bilateral predicate can name.
#
# At @smarts altitude (per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4): smarts is a
# record with magic_form: magic_contract. At @magic altitude (per
# magic.mirror #80): magic_contract is the form/process-substrate
# record {surface, mechanism, promise}. The projection IS field
# access at substrate-decl altitude; the lift preserves byte-equality
# identity at the projected field.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
magic_form_of(s: smarts) -> magic_contract { \ }

# === magic_as_smarts adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a @magic contract
# to a @smarts integration with the magic_form field populated. The
# other smarts fields (frame_form, cyberpunk_form, beam_form,
# cybernetic_extra, kintsugi_form) are populated as default refs at
# the lift altitude; consumer species that need the other fields
# populated substantively use the other @smarts/<family> adapters
# (forward-promised).
#
# Per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4 + Seam-precedent: the @smarts
# integration IS a typed record; the magic_form projection is the
# substrate-pull-correct lift surface. The adapter completes the
# round-trip at the magic_form field altitude:
#   magic_form_of(magic_as_smarts(mc)) = mc
# for all magic_contract mc. This is the cheapest falsification
# check; failure here means the adapter is mis-implemented.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
magic_as_smarts(mc: magic_contract) -> smarts { \ }

# === smarts_promise adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action extracting the @magic
# invariant (the promise) from a @smarts integration. The promise IS
# the magic_form's promise field at the substrate altitude; this
# extraction EXPOSES it as a substrate-decl operation the bilateral
# predicate can name in invariant_preserved.
#
# Equivalent to magic_form_of(s).promise at the substrate-decl level;
# named separately because the bilateral predicate consumes it as a
# typed parameter, and the substrate-decl is cleaner when each
# adapter operation is named explicitly per [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
smarts_promise(s: smarts) -> magic_invariant { \ }

# === smarts_satisfies_magic bilateral predicate ===
#
# THE CROSS-FAMILY BILATERAL PREDICATE in @smarts that discharges
# BOTH parent-family AND child-family verdicts in one clause. The
# substrate-pull-correct way to mechanically discharge the
# form/process-substrate-altitude composition claim that the @smarts
# family-root preserved as forward-promised at #83.
#
# Two `requires` clauses, both load-bearing:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p)
#      — the @smarts family-root predicate. Discharges that the
#      @smarts integration maintains substrate-architectural
#      discipline-flexibility under perturbation; the boundary
#      harness at @io audits this per recognition #57.
#
#   2. invariant_preserved(magic_form_of(s), smarts_promise(s))
#      — the @magic/contract family-root predicate. Discharges that
#      the @smarts integration's magic_form has its promise preserved
#      by the contract under the boundary harness at @io.
#
# Both must hold for the smarts integration to satisfy @magic at
# substrate altitude. The cross-family composition mechanically
# discharges the form/process-substrate identity claim that the
# magic_form: magic_contract typed-field carries at @smarts
# integration altitude.
#
# The signature takes smarts and perturbation as explicit typed
# parameters per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] because the consumer
# species name these at the typed boundary.
#
# Consumer species (forward-promised @smarts species shards
# implementing the four Models; @spectral/garden/smarts hosted
# deployment) name this predicate when their operation requires
# cross-family discharge.
smarts_satisfies_magic(s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
requires invariant_preserved(magic_form_of(s), smarts_promise(s))
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge per @magic/frame + @smarts/pack precedent ===
#
# This adapter closes the magic_form-projection altitude of
# "@smarts integrates @magic at substrate altitude":
#  - magic_contract ↔ smarts.magic_form round-trips via
#    magic_as_smarts / magic_form_of.
#  - The bilateral smarts_satisfies_magic discharges BOTH family
#    predicates simultaneously.
#
# It does NOT close round-trip identity at the smarts-as-whole
# altitude. Given a smarts s with all six form-fields populated,
# magic_as_smarts(magic_form_of(s)) discards s.frame_form,
# s.cyberpunk_form, s.beam_form, s.cybernetic_extra, s.kintsugi_form.
# Other @smarts/<family> adapters cover those fields.
#
# Honest claim post-adapter:
#  - "@smarts integrates @magic at magic_form altitude" — CLOSED.
#  - "@smarts integrates @magic at smarts-as-whole altitude" —
#    FORWARD-PROMISED pending the full cross-family adapter set.

out @smarts/magic
out magic_form_of
out magic_as_smarts
out smarts_promise
out smarts_satisfies_magic
